{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars","id":120518,"title":"Star Wars EU: more Exalted than Star Wars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-27T14:12:18-07:00","id":120518,"title":"Star Wars EU: more Exalted than Star Wars?","content":"On another forum, there's an arguement going about the meritw of Timothy Zah's Thrawn Trilogy. In jt someone said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well... it is only really the gold standard because compared to some of the other books that followed, it was not terrible. They weren't perfect... nothing is. But while it had jedi... it didn't revolve around the jedi. It had political intrigue, underworld adventures, and military operations. Later books often revolved entirely around magical samurai space wizards and their slap fight amongst themselves over which group of a handful of privileged godlings based on a very nebulous binary belief system over who gets to rule over the countless trillions of others who don't have a magic laser sword. </div> </div> </div>Almost sounds like he's describing Exalted there. What do you think? Does the EU feel mkre like Exalted than what Star Wars once was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:18:59-07:00","id":120522,"title":"","content":"Some of the fights I've had in 2e felt like the fights in the prequel trilogy.<br /> <br /> That is to say, the fights went on so long that they took all tension out of the scene and dropped you out of any sense of verisimilitude.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:19:28-07:00","id":120524,"title":"","content":"Well the post-Zahn era has certainly gone down the toilet in much the same fashion as early 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T20:11:05-07:00","id":120691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120522#post120522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some of the fights I've had in 2e felt like the fights in the prequel trilogy.<br /> <br /> That is to say, the fights went on so long that they took all tension out of the scene and dropped you out of any sense of verisimilitude.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way. We constantly have to re-iterate out stunts after we're done rolling because it took so long to get from A to Z, and it feels a little lacking by then since we just had to watch it through the lens of number crunching in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","user":"Foorish Shamurai","date":". 04-27-2014, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T23:03:25-07:00","id":120776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars#post120518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another forum, there's an arguement going about the meritw of Timothy Zah's Thrawn Trilogy. In jt someone said this:</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, that made me giggle. It's pretty accurate. <br /> <br /> I was a fan of Star Wars in spite of the Jedi, not because of them. I always found the non-Jedi characters, like Han Solo or (EU) Boba Fett to be far more interesting than any of the Force using characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T23:27:55-07:00","id":120792,"title":"","content":"I love Star Wars, i love the EU, i do enjoy Jedi based stories but i don't think SW should only be about jedi. I find the late 90's PC games the best as they treated jedi as a rare and special aspect. Look at the WEG 2nd edtion becoming a jedi is fricken hard, but that makes the story interesting. Exalted on the other hand is to me about being larger than life, where star wars in the WEG sense was part of exploring a galaxy that was way larger than a 1000 games could ever cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/694-firemage","name":"Firemage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar694_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T01:11:17-07:00","id":120828,"title":"","content":"Jedi are awesome(And the Sith creed), but that's all there is to it to the Star Wars universe. <br /> <br /> Each story is about a Jedi going Sith, or a Sith going Jedi. All the damn time, everything 'important' in this setting is the binary mystic teaching and people going around the Face-Heel Revolving door. <br /> <br /> I don't like comparing it to Exalted, because everything in it is less than anything Creation has to offer - as a setting, as moral dilemmas, as power scale, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> magical samurai space wizards and their slap fight amongst themselves over which group of a handful of privileged godlings based on a very nebulous binary belief system over who gets to rule over the countless trillions of others who don't have a magic laser sword. </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that this is a proper description of Exalted. <br /> <br /> People I play RPG with think of Exalted as something like an exaggerated kitchen sink in the way that they don't see it as a serious setting, all because of those little 'mush random fun words around' tidbits around the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T01:37:04-07:00","id":120839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120828#post120828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jedi are awesome(And the Sith creed), but that's all there is to it to the Star Wars universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even really like Star Wars and I can tell this is not an accurate summary of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2031-savior-girl","name":"Savior Girl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2031_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T01:59:12-07:00","id":120844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120828#post120828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that this is a proper description of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the entirety of that post is a proper description of the HISTORY of Exalted. Exalted started off as something deep and interesting and eventually, over the span of 2e, kinda devolved into over-the-top anime action insanity with a giant robot sun. Here's hoping that both SW's coming reboot of the EU and Ex3 both bring things back on course!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T05:34:00-07:00","id":120889,"title":"","content":"The history of Exalted is way more complex and interesting than the one in Star Wars, in both 1st edition and 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Really, on a big scale, the only thing that matters and is distinct is the duality between the Light side and the Dark side. If you remove the Force, you get a generic sci-fi setting. If you remove the Force, you make the setting into a generic boring setting without any deepness. If you remove one element from Exalted, you still get Exalted.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Force is like the generic Good/Evil in DnD. You serve one, or you serve the other. Objective moral forces in the world make for a boring story.<br /> Star Wars actually is very similar to Warhammer 40K. Both are one-trick ponies. Warhammer's main staple is 'Never ending war and misery' <br /> <br /> - If you play a Star Wars you are a Jedi/Sith and the story is you being tempted or you redeem yourself.<br /> - If you play Warhammer, you Burn The Heretics. <br /> <br /> That's all about it for these 2 settings. They are not made as a coherent working world, they do not deserve to be compared with Exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T06:20:05-07:00","id":120901,"title":"","content":"Star Wars is originally only about Jedi vs Sith. The movies are a straight-up good vs evil conflict; there is no geopolitics more complex than &quot;Empire = Bad, Rebels = Good.&quot; Insofar as the EU is better about this, it is more like Exalted. However the setting still revolves around the Jedi and Sith, particularly in the NJO era and onwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:15:51-07:00","id":120970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120889#post120889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of Exalted is way more complex and interesting than the one in Star Wars, in both 1st edition and 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Really, on a big scale, the only thing that matters and is distinct is the duality between the Light side and the Dark side. If you remove the Force, you get a generic sci-fi setting. If you remove the Force, you make the setting into a generic boring setting without any deepness. If you remove one element from Exalted, you still get Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> SW is &quot;Science Fantasy&quot;, basically a fairy tale with a vaguely science-based form of &quot;magic&quot;, which is the main thing that sets it apart from all the other SF stories out there. Not saying that you can't have compelling non-Force using characters, engaged in good drama, just that there's no reason those stories couldn't be told in some other property. <br /> <br /> And the overall story of SW is Good vs. Evil, expressing itself through the Light and Dark Sides of the Force, which uses the Jedi and Sith to play out this conflict (who themselves use the Rebellion and Empire as tools). That kind of simplistic, dualistic tone doesn't really work for Exalted, except maybe for some parts of late 2E.<br /> <br /> Having said all that, I'm not gonna join the hate train for the EU. I can't claim to have read ALL of them, and I certainly have issues with their obvious flaws, but on the whole, I think it is a solid continuation of the series, and have enjoyed most of the ones I have picked up, esp the ones set during the Old Republic and Clone Wars. I'm glad that Disney just announced that they aren't discontinuing the series, which I was almost certain they were going to do, deciding to respect a continuity that so many fans invested so much into! Reveals good things about Disney's stewardship of SW, hopefully...<br /> <br /> As to Luke Skywalker himself, he has grown so gorram powerful, fulfilling the word-of-god that he is THE most powerful Force-user ever (sorry, Darth Bane fans!) that he was taking head-on what was basically a Primordial in the latest storyline<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:07:27-07:00","id":121091,"title":"","content":"It's not that I hate it, it's just too simplistic. <br /> <br /> @Hand-of-Omega: Which is this storyline? Is it in a comic, or a novel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:12:04-07:00","id":121096,"title":"","content":"Series of novels. He basically ends up taking on what amounts to a horrible monstrosity in the Force (Note: NOT the representation of the Dark Side as some claim, Abeloth is... something that should have never been), along with Darth Krayt, neatly tying in the old Dark Horse comics with the EU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:32:56-07:00","id":121115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars#post120518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another forum, there's an arguement going about the meritw of Timothy Zah's Thrawn Trilogy. In jt someone said this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Almost sounds like he's describing Exalted there. What do you think? Does the EU feel mkre like Exalted than what Star Wars once was?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the description given of the EU novels (and the Jedi) is not very accurate or fair. While the series had it ups and downs, I consider it to have ended on a high note. And I don't think it has much resemblence to Exalted beyond the tropes of a fantasy action story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:50:55-07:00","id":121137,"title":"","content":"Well, Darth Nihilus was a sort of non-giant Force Galactus, so I'm not surprised by some sort of Force Abomination That Was Not Meant To Be. And depending on what material you consider, Anakin is either Force Jesus or Son of Mad Force Science. Then there is superweapon after superweapon trying to top the last one, <i>starting </i>with the Deathstar. In short, Star Wars has jumped the shark several times ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:56:50-07:00","id":121143,"title":"","content":"Space Opera does indeed have several elements of style in common with the Mythical Wuxia Drama that is Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:57:26-07:00","id":121144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120889#post120889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history of Exalted is way more complex and interesting than the one in Star Wars, in both 1st edition and 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Really, on a big scale, the only thing that matters and is distinct is the duality between the Light side and the Dark side. If you remove the Force, you get a generic sci-fi setting. If you remove the Force, you make the setting into a generic boring setting without any deepness. If you remove one element from Exalted, you still get Exalted.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Force is like the generic Good/Evil in DnD. You serve one, or you serve the other. Objective moral forces in the world make for a boring story.<br /> Star Wars actually is very similar to Warhammer 40K. Both are one-trick ponies. Warhammer's main staple is 'Never ending war and misery'<br /> <br /> - If you play a Star Wars you are a Jedi/Sith and the story is you being tempted or you redeem yourself.<br /> - If you play Warhammer, you Burn The Heretics.<br /> <br /> That's all about it for these 2 settings. They are not made as a coherent working world, they do not deserve to be compared with Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really true, though. At all. There's a LOT more to Star Wars than just the Jedi and the Sith, and early EU stuff proves it pretty handily. There's a reason why Timothy Zahn's stuff is beloved.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I've got a feeling this thread might get borderline in a hurry though so we might want to consider having it pre-moved already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:59:28-07:00","id":121145,"title":"","content":"The Heir to the Empire trilogy is top-tier stuff, and among the best ever produced by anyone in the Star Wars EU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:36:45-07:00","id":121216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121145#post121145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Heir to the Empire trilogy is top-tier stuff, and among the best ever produced by anyone in the Star Wars EU.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye it is good. it's too bad it's not canon any longer for Star Wars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:35:40-07:00","id":121265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a shame, but there was just so much <i>crap</i> writing in the EU that I can understand their decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T22:40:14-07:00","id":121505,"title":"","content":"Let's face it: It was inevitable. They already demonstrated they didn't much care for the EU when they wrote the prequels. Now that they're doing sequels, they're running into a <i>huge</i> amount of pre-existing material. Their options were either A) consign themselves to doing EU adaptations forever or B) just declare the whole thing non-canon. I can't see how anyone's surprised with what they chose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T22:47:12-07:00","id":121508,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the thread title, I can honestly say that at least one EU title, <i>Splinter of the Mind's Eye</i>, feels extremely like Exalted. This is likely because of the very high concentration of pulp in that novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T01:43:08-07:00","id":121564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121216#post121216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye it is good. it's too bad it's not canon any longer for Star Wars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just on the off chance that the new movies would have referenced it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T04:23:39-07:00","id":121610,"title":"","content":"Never liked most ofthe Zahn stuff, tried to make Star Wars more into military science fiction instead of it's more fun pulp roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:42:29-07:00","id":121790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120889#post120889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Star Wars actually is very similar to Warhammer 40K. Both are one-trick ponies. Warhammer's main staple is 'Never ending war and misery'<br /> <br /> - If you play a Star Wars you are a Jedi/Sith and the story is you being tempted or you redeem yourself.<br /> - If you play Warhammer, you Burn The Heretics.<br /> <br /> That's all about it for these 2 settings. They are not made as a coherent working world, they do not deserve to be compared with Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree with that. Yes, the fiction in GW's hands has largely become a repetitive parody of itself (Kaldor Marysue Draigo!), but there's still a lot of good stuff out there in novels &amp; RPG's, that makes the universe much more nuanced and expansive than the war-skullz-shoulderpads-grimdark that the wargame focuses on. In particular, the Fantasy Flight RPG's have some amazing material out there, and I seriously think that <i>Rogue Trader</i> in some ways explores the theme of corrupting power better than <i>Exalted</i> does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:46:32-07:00","id":121795,"title":"","content":"The problem with Warhammer's fiction is it becomes very clear that it is written mostly by people who have never once had any sort of position of authority or power of their own. This becomes <i>very</i> apparent when you realize that one of the undertones of just about every book is &quot;Man, everyone who has any sort of temporal power whatsoever inevitably is a jerk, a Chaos cultist, or an utter bastard.&quot; It's very one note, and made especially bad in shit like every time the Grey Knights show up and basically murder everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T09:57:07-07:00","id":121805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=120828#post120828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jedi are awesome(And the Sith creed), but that's all there is to it to the Star Wars universe.<br /> <br /> Each story is about a Jedi going Sith, or a Sith going Jedi. All the damn time, everything 'important' in this setting is the binary mystic teaching and people going around the Face-Heel Revolving door.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only there was a well known MMO based in the Star Wars universe that has both 7 individual story lines not centered around Jedi turning Sith or Sith turning Jedi as well as the ongoing story about the war between the Empire and Republic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars#post120518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost sounds like he's describing Exalted there. What do you think? Does the EU feel mkre like Exalted than what Star Wars once was?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sith Empire is ruled over by a group of superpowered beings who hold themselves as naturally superior to those below them and constantly squabble among themselves for power. It promotes slavery, aggressive expansion, the exploitation of conquered lands, and is ruled over by a centuries old Emperor who has not been seen for some time.<br /> <br /> The Empire has recently suffered great losses as members of the Dark Council sabotage their rivals and cripple the war effort. However, a young, ambitious, and 'idealistic' general has recently risen in power and popularity. He wants to put an end to the in-fighting and strengthen the Empire... by rebuilding it without an all-powerful Emperor.<br /> <br /> That reminds me of something in Exalted...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 04-29-2014, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:57:25-07:00","id":121854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121805#post121805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If only there was a well known MMO based in the Star Wars universe that has both 7 individual story lines not centered around Jedi turning Sith or Sith turning Jedi as well as the ongoing story about the war between the Empire and Republic.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, if only such a game existed. Perhaps we could set it back in time somewhere. Hmm, maybe during the Great Hyperspace War? Nah. Oh! I know! We could set it in the Republic! Maybe even call it Star Wars: The Republic!<br /> <br /> Hm... wait, that sounds kind of familiar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:03:16-07:00","id":121859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121795#post121795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Warhammer's fiction is it becomes very clear that it is written mostly by people who have never once had any sort of position of authority or power of their own. This becomes <i>very</i> apparent when you realize that one of the undertones of just about every book is &quot;Man, everyone who has any sort of temporal power whatsoever inevitably is a jerk, a Chaos cultist, or an utter bastard.&quot; It's very one note, and made especially bad in shit like every time the Grey Knights show up and basically murder everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not as if Exalted hasn't had that same tendency, you must admit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:10:04-07:00","id":121868,"title":"","content":"A tendency, yes. In 40k basically <i>anyone</i> in power is an utter dick, secretly serves Chaos, or is a Tau spy. Or a Grey Knight, but they're a special kind of terrible writing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: No, seriously, the Grey Knights are fucking dumb. &quot;Oh, looks like the Grey Knights are going to be getting into a battle soon. Time to find another planet full of people who'd qualify as saints to butcher so we can coat their armor and bullets in their blood.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":374,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","user":"Nocte ex Mortis","date":". 04-29-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:08:24-07:00","id":121931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121859#post121859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not as if Exalted hasn't had that same tendency, you must admit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, White Wolf is more egalitarian. It's less &quot;people in power are assholes&quot; and more &quot;everyone who is given the opportunity is an asshole&quot; :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T10:48:06-07:00","id":123863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121505#post121505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's face it: It was inevitable. They already demonstrated they didn't much care for the EU when they wrote the prequels. Now that they're doing sequels, they're running into a <i>huge</i> amount of pre-existing material. Their options were either A) consign themselves to doing EU adaptations forever or B) just declare the whole thing non-canon. I can't see how anyone's surprised with what they chose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not, and I liked a lot of what the EU did. But even if they didn't do straight up adaptations, they'd be creatively hobbling themselves if they left it in continuity. If I were making a new series, I'd make the same choice, even if I were a bigger fan of it than I am.<br /> <br /> What *does* surprise me is the recent announcement they made about the EU. Unless I misread it, they are still continuing the series, just as a non-canonical &quot;alternate reality&quot;. If true, then that's pretty cool of them, even if it means two separate book lines being published...<br /> <br /> I know this isn't in the Exalted group anymore, but whatever. I always was reminded of how Jedi use the Force by some of the ways Essence works with the Exalted (esp how it is described as aiding in their Dodge Def). Maybe the SW galaxy is one where Shinmaic interaction is different enough that it gave Essence sort of a semi-consciousness, so that it can act through people and even subtly arrange events?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}